  "body": "In speccing JS module loading, I associated the module map with the environment settings object. I believe at the time I blanked out on the fact that environment settings objects are 1:1 with browsing contexts, not with Windows. Thus, the current spec requires persisting the module map across navigations. This seems quite bad.\n\nContrast with images, which are cached on the document: https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#list-of-available-images\n\nI should fix this, I guess by having Window and WorkerGlobalScope objects each have module maps?\n\n@ajklein @jonco3 just want to confirm that I am correct that the current spec is bonkers and you were not planning on implementing it.\n",
